menu "IGPP display"

    config IGPP_COLUMN_PERIOD_TENTHS_US
        int "Column period, 0.1 us units"
        range 100 10000
        default 1512
        help
            Time between two columns of the scan. 96 columns make one frame.
            The default (151.2 us) is TA0CCR0 = 906 at SMCLK 24 MHz / 4 from the
            MSP430 firmware in master. It must be replaced with the value measured
            on the running display (golden capture): the anode pulse doublers
            only work with the original timing.

    config IGPP_SPI_CLOCK_HZ
        int "Anode SPI clock, Hz"
        range 100000 20000000
        default 6000000
        help
            MSP430 firmware: SMCLK 24 MHz / 4 = 6 MHz. Confirm with the capture.

    config IGPP_STALL_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Scan stall timeout, ms"
        range 10 1000
        default 50
        help
            If no frame completes for this long, the cathodes are deselected and
            the chip reboots.

endmenu
